  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The bond joining two successive nucleotides in the same strand of DNA is called the phosphodiester bond. the phosphodiester bond is the linkage between the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>3</mn><mo>'</mo></msup></math> carbon atom of one sugar molecule and the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>5</mn><mo>'</mo></msup></math> carbon atom of another, deoxyribose in DNA and ribose in RNA.</p><p>Phosphodiester linkage</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/1bb632fb-cc8c-46e1-9d7e-84c39a0b994f.png\" style=\"width: 408px; height: 470px;\"/></p>",
